# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the prefill SDPA programme's oneq jobs (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a
# throwaway commit of tp4/fusion-1 (a branch that carries optimisation/ttnn-op/sdpa_prefill_oneq) and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. ONE TAG AT A TIME; wait for the run to
# finish; never cancel a running card job. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. A placeholder in @...@ is filled in by whoever drives the
# window (@SERVED_IMAGE@: the served image's reference; @K64J_OQ_GRAFT_DIR@ and @K64J_OQ_TTNNCPP_SHA256@: the K64j-OQ graft directory and its binary's digest, the K64J_OQ_TTNNCPP_SHA256 line of
# L1). C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the window's own image: the ONE fusion image, built by OQ-B0 (the fusion pack's B0 with C2_BAKE_GRAFT=K64j-OQ) from the pushed branch head
# (sed -i 's/tp4-fusion-1/<tag>/' *.env). ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the read rules and the minutes.
# T4 (TIMED, four cards, the solo TTFT pair of the oneq lever on the fusion image): prefill_ladder_solo - four real-code prompts of about 4,096 / 32,768 / 131,072 / 253,920 tokens, ONE request at a time with nothing else running, a 16-token answer - on the combined arm plus QWEN_FAST_SDPA_PF_ONEQ=1 (the -fx-all-oneq twin, repeat). The lever acts in PREFILL, so this pair (not the decode-round ABAB of the generated ONEQ jobs)
# is its end-to-end measurement; the ladder's time to first token at the 131,072 and 253,920 rungs is what the estimate is about (est. solo TTFT -7.9 s and -29.8 s; the unprofiled twin measured 36.77 s at 131,072
# and the 254k rung is about 98 s).
# THE PAIR: T1 control, T2 oneq, T3 control, T4 oneq (ABAB, every boot a fresh reset, one tag at a time). THE CONTROL IS THE COMBINED ARM, THE LEVER IS THE COMBINED ARM PLUS ONEQ: both boots run the SAME
# image (OQ-B0's, the K64j-OQ binary) and the same fifteen fx-all levers; the only difference is QWEN_FAST_SDPA_PF_ONEQ=1, so the pair measures the lever on top of the fusion programme and nothing else.
# READ: c2_smoke_check clean (a oneq boot also has its '[PINDIAG] sdpa prefill oneq engaged' line and no fell-back line; a control boot has none), no stall; then
# python3 -B scripts/ci/prefill_ladder_report.py <T1 results> --second <T2 results> and the same for (T3, T4): the TTFT of the oneq arm over the control's per rung (a ratio below 1 is oneq faster) and the
# answer text of every rung equal between the arms. Card M measured the per-layer SDPA at 0.50x of the served call at 131k..254k (0.72x at 4k); estimated TTFT ratios about 0.79 at the 131,072 rung and about
# 0.69 at 253,920 (the 4k rung and the 32k rung move by under a second). The control-to-control floor is T1 against T3. Nothing here gates: one pair is one pair.
# REQUIRES: the image is OQ-B0's (a K64j image refuses the oneq boot at the first chain call: 'lacks the oneq edits'); the admission accepts the K64j-OQ binary in a gate boot (this is one).
# TIMED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this job; no build, no CI push, no other job beside it. Duration (estimate): boot 10 minutes, solo ladder 4 (about 98 s for the 254k rung), 25 minutes in all; the box is 40.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-all-oneq
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,prefill_ladder_solo
C2_SMOKE_PARTIAL=solo prefill ladder for the oneq TTFT pair: its test list is fixed by the protocol, so concurrent8_steady is not run
C2_BOX_MINUTES=40
